@startuml AD_Redistribution
title UC-F04 + UC-F05 - Plan and Complete Vehicle Redistribution
|Operator|
start
:Select vehicles, source Hub and destination Hub;
|System / Controller|
:Check Operator permission;
fork
  |Database|
  :Read current vehicle states and commitments;
fork again
  |Database|
  :Read source/destination status and capacity;
end fork
|System / Controller|
:Validate feasibility (UC-S03);
if (Data current and transfer feasible?) then (yes)
  |Operator|
  :Review transfer summary;
  if (Confirm assignment?) then (yes)
    |System / Controller|
    :Revalidate against current state;
    if (Still feasible?) then (yes)
      |Database|
      :Atomically save assignment and vehicle commitments;
      |System / Controller|
      if (Save successful?) then (yes)
        :Show Assigned order;
        |Operator|
        :Arrange physical transfer outside the system;
        :Select order and confirmed arrived vehicles;
        |System / Controller|
        :Check order state and vehicle identities;
        if (Arrivals valid?) then (yes)
          |Database|
          :Atomically update arrived vehicle locations,
          Hub occupancy and order progress;
          |System / Controller|
          if (Update committed?) then (yes)
            if (All vehicles arrived?) then (yes)
              :Show Completed order;
            else (no)
              :Show PartiallyCompleted order;
            endif
          else (no)
            :Show failure; retain last confirmed state;
          endif
        else (no)
          :Reject mismatch or duplicate confirmation;
        endif
      else (no)
        :Show save error; no order exists;
      endif
    else (no)
      :Reject stale proposal and show reason;
    endif
  else (no)
    :Leave state unchanged;
  endif
else (no)
  :Show ineligible vehicles, stale data or capacity error;
endif
stop
note right
Creating an order never asserts physical arrival.
Only confirmed arrivals change location and occupancy.
end note
@enduml
